{
  "raw_html": "<button type='button' role='link' class='btn btn-link p-0 text-start' id='link_0' aria-label=\" Talari Naresh versus The State of Telangana pdf\"  class='noToken' href='#' onclick=javascript:open_pdf('0','2026','2026_6_294_310','2026INSC486'); ><font size='4'> <strong>TALARI NARESH<span class='fst-italic'> versus </span>THE STATE OF TELANGANA </strong>- <span class='escrText'>[2026] 6 S.C.R. 294</span><span class='ncDisplay'>2026 INSC 486</span><input type='hidden' id='cnr' value=ESCR010001692026></button></font><br><strong>Coram : PRASHANT KUMAR MISHRA<sup style=\"color: #268e97;font-size: 22px;top: 0;\" class=\"tooltip-sup\" data-tooltip=\"Author\">*</sup></strong><br> Issue for Consideration The present appeal by the appellant-convict is directed against judgment and order dated 04.02.2025 of the High Court. Thereby, the High Court confirmed the conviction and sentence against the appellant and held the appellant guilty of commission of offences u/ss.302 and and 3(1)(x) of SC/ST Act. Headnotes&dagger; Penal Code, 1860 &ndash; ss.302 and 323 &ndash; Scheduled Castes and The Scheduled Tribes (Prevention of Atrocities) Act, 1989 &ndash; ss.3(2)(v) and 3(1)(x) &ndash; On 14.02.2013, victim-deceased had eloped with appellant&rsquo;s younger sister<br><strong class='caseDetailsTD' ><span style='color:#212F3D' > Decision Date :</span><font color='green'> 13-05-2026</font><span style='color:#212F3D' > | Case No :</span><font color='green'> CRIMINAL APPEAL No. 2506/2026</font><span style='color:#212F3D' > | Disposal Nature :</span><font color='green'> Appeal(s) allowed</font>   <span style='color:#212F3D' > |  Bench :</span><font color='green'> 2 Judges</font></strong><div class='row my-1 mt-2 border bg-light'><div class='col-auto'><a href='#' class='btn btn-outline-secondary btn-sm my-1' onclick=open_splitview('0','2026','2026_6_294_310','2026INSC486','S')><i <i class='fas fa-columns me-2'></i>Split view</a></div><div class='col-auto'><a href='#' class='bt